          SPC flooring is sold on one promise: a rigid, waterproof plank that clicks together over almost any flat subfloor. The promise is mostly true, and the exceptions all live in the details nobody prints on the front of the box. This guide covers the seven lines we would price first, and then the numbers that matter far more than the brand name.
        </p>

        <QuickPicks products={PRODUCTS} />

        <div id="what-is-spc" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. What SPC Flooring Actually Is
          </h2>

          <p>
            SPC stands for stone plastic composite. The core of each plank is a dense board made mostly of limestone powder bound with PVC and stabilizers, and that mineral content is the whole point. Where flexible luxury vinyl bends with the subfloor underneath it, an SPC plank behaves more like a thin tile: stiff, dimensionally stable and resistant to the dents that soft vinyl picks up under furniture feet.
          </p>

          <p>
            On top of that core sits a printed vinyl film that carries the wood or stone pattern, then a clear wear layer that takes the abuse, then usually a UV-cured coating. Underneath, most click-together SPC planks have a thin attached pad of cork or foam. Because the core is rigid and the edges are machined into a locking profile, the floor floats without glue, which is why SPC became the default do-it-yourself choice for kitchens, basements and rentals.
          </p>

          <p>
            It is worth being clear about what SPC is not. It is not laminate, which has a wood-fiber core that swells if water gets in, a distinction covered in <a href="/is-laminate-flooring-waterproof/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">our guide to whether laminate is waterproof</a>. It is not a tile you can stand heavy loads on without a proper subfloor, and it is not immune to heat. Those limits shape every buying decision below.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you already know you want a vinyl plank and are comparing brands across the whole category, our broader roundup of the <a href="/best-vinyl-plank-flooring/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">best vinyl plank flooring</a> is the place to start. This page narrows the question to the rigid-core subset and goes deeper on construction, because that is where cheap and good diverge. For below-grade rooms in particular, see our <a href="/best-flooring-for-basement/" class="text-[#1E90FF] font-bold hover:underline">best flooring for basements</a> guide, which covers moisture testing before any plank goes down.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Picks -->
        <div id="top-picks" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            2. The 7 Best SPC Flooring Lines Worth Pricing
          </h2>

          <p>
            These picks are ranked on construction, warranty structure and how well each line fits a specific job, using manufacturer specifications rather than our own lab numbers. The product links are affiliate links, which means we earn a commission if you buy through them, at no extra cost to you. Specs change between collections, so confirm core thickness, wear layer and pad details on the listing for the exact color you choose.
          </p>

          {PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => (
            <div id={product.id} class="scroll-mt-24 mt-12 first:mt-8">
              <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow">
                <div class="bg-gray-900 px-6 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
